    "answer": {
      "short": "No values of $p$ and $q$ make this a uniform probability distribution.",
      "worked": "For a uniform distribution, the three probabilities must be equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q+2&=p-2q+5\\\\3q&=3\\\\q&=1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}p-2q+5&=2p-3q\\\\p-2+5&=2p-3\\\\p&=6\\end{align*}$$\nThese values make each entry equal to $9$, so their sum is $27$, rather than $1$. A uniform probability distribution on three outcomes requires each probability to be $\\frac13$. Therefore, no values of $p$ and $q$ satisfy the question.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
